  <content>
    <section>
    <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this
              lesson.</para>
            <para>For questions 1 - 2, use the following scenario to identify the equation
              described.</para>
            <para><quote>Two different telephone carriers offer the following plans that a person is
              considering. Company A has a monthly fee of $20 and charges $0.05/minute for calls.
              Company B has a monthly fee of $5 and charges $0.10/minute for calls.</quote></para>

        <exercise id="_7d1d5fe2-34d3-4b58-b950-b8f1569aaf7c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Find the model for the entire  cost, c,  when Company A’s plan is used for m
              minutes.</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(c=20 + 0.05m\)</para>
            <para>\(c= 5 + 0.10m\)</para>
            <para>\(c= 20 + 0.10m\)</para>
            <para>\(c=5+ 0.05m\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is c=20 + 0.05m.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="fdcc69e8-e6b8-4757-8482-f965eaf43aea" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Find the model for the entire cost, c, when  Company B’s plan is used for m
              minutes.</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(c=20 + 0.05m\)</para>
            <para>\(c= 5 + 0.10m\)</para>
            <para>\(c= 20 + 0.10m\)</para>
            <para>\(c=5+ 0.05m\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is b. c= 5 + 0.10m.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="b9826d19-a329-447c-b724-3006ce30ff6d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>If a carpenter sawed a 10-ft board into two sections and one section was n ft
              long, how long would the other section, S, be in terms of n ?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(S=\frac{10}n\)</para>
            <para>\(S=10-n\)</para>
            <para>\(S=10-2n\)</para>
            <para>\(S=\frac{10}2n\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is S=10-n.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

<para>Use the table below for problems 4 and 5:</para>
            <para><quote>Tyler needs to complete this table for his consumer science class. He knows
              that 1 tablespoon contains 3 teaspoons and that 1 cup contains 16 tablespoons.</quote></para>
            <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
              <tgroup cols="3"><tbody><row>
                  <entry>a. ____
                  </entry>
                  <entry>b. ____
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para>2</para>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <para>36</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para>12</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>c. ____
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>d. ____
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para>48</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para>3</para>
                  </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody></tgroup></table>


        <exercise id="_02155fb4-2142-451f-b47b-3794b757c877" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For each of the missing spaces in the table above, a-d, select the missing
              value that helps complete the table.</para>
            <para>a.________</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(\frac34\)</para>
            <para>32</para>
            <para>64</para>
            <para>96</para>
            <para>144</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 96.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="e073cd7e-6a31-4135-ad9c-2fb461b3d392" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>b.________</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(\frac34\)</para>
            <para>32</para>
            <para>64</para>
            <para>96</para>
            <para>144</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 32.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="_01389e45-0f85-49f5-ab9c-a627dd91487e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>c.________</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(\frac34\)</para>
            <para>32</para>
            <para>64</para>
            <para>96</para>
            <para>144</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(\frac34\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="_487b241e-1926-4620-b221-e8022719898d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>d.________</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(\frac34\)</para>
            <para>32</para>
            <para>64</para>
            <para>96</para>
            <para>144</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 144.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="_4c5a24e4-2130-4cb9-a292-f9af235512dd" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Choose the equation that represents the number of teaspoons, t, contained in a
              cup, C.</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(c = 48t\)</para>
            <para>\(c=\frac t{48}\)</para>
            <para>\(c = t-48\)</para>
            <para>\(c=\frac t3\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is (c=\frac t{48}\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="_5cc7c5b1-deb6-422d-998d-0274bdde0e79" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The volume of dry goods, like apples or peaches, can be measured using bushels,
              pecks, and quarts. A bushel contains 4 pecks, and a peck contains 8 quarts. What is
              the relationship between the number of bushels, b, and the number of quarts, q?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(b=\frac q{32}\)</para>
            <para>\(b=\frac q{12}\)</para>
            <para>\(b=\frac q{64}\)</para>
            <para>\(b=32q\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.3.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(b=\frac q{32}\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
    </section>
